The '''1956 NFL draft''' had its first three rounds held on November 28, 1955, at [[the Bellevue-Stratford Hotel]] in [[Philadelphia]], [[Pennsylvania]], and its final twenty-seven rounds on January 17–18, 1956, at the [[Ambassador Hotel (Los Angeles)|Ambassador Hotel]] in [[Los Angeles]], [[California]]<ref name="NFLgeo">{{cite web |url=http://www.footballgeography.com/nfl-draft-sites/ |title=NFL Draft Locations |author=<!--Staff writer(s); no by-line.--> |date=October 2, 2014 |website=www.footballgeography.com |access-date=2014-10-23 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20150905090250/http://www.footballgeography.com/nfl-draft-sites/ |archive-date=2015-09-05 |url-status=dead }}</ref><ref>{{cite news|last1=Salomone|first1=Dan|title=NFL Draft headed to Chicago in 2015|url=http://www.giants.com/news-and-blogs/article-1/NFL-Draft-headed-to-Chicago-in-2015/3ac322b1-3b4c-4a16-aba7-6e08d31b1756|access-date=June 3, 2015|publisher=[[New York Giants]]|work=Giants.com|date=October 2, 2014|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20150930065327/http://www.giants.com/news-and-blogs/article-1/NFL-Draft-headed-to-Chicago-in-2015/3ac322b1-3b4c-4a16-aba7-6e08d31b1756|archive-date=2015-09-30|url-status=dead}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |title=Draft Diaries: Vikings Consultant was Asleep When Picked by Browns in '56 |url=https://www.vikings.com/news/draft-diaries-vikings-consultant-was-asleep-when-picked-by-browns-in-56 |date=23 April 2020 |last=Peters |first=Craig |website=Minnesota Vikings |access-date=23 April 2025}}</ref>

The previous NFL drafts in the 1950s were held in January; the first three rounds (37 selections) were moved up this year to late November to better compete with teams {{nowrap|from [[Canadian Football League|Canada]].<ref name=ppnflbg>{{cite news |url=https://news.google.com/newspapers?id=GGAbAAAAIBAJ&sjid=4U0EAAAAIBAJ&pg=6328%2C3604543 |newspaper=Pittsburgh Press |agency=United Press |title=NFL will begin draft tomorrow |date=November 27, 1955 |page=3, section 4}}</ref><ref name=eartod>{{cite news |url=https://news.google.com/newspapers?id=v2hQAAAAIBAJ&sjid=CxAEAAAAIBAJ&pg=4747%2C5145927 |work=Milwaukee Sentinel |agency=Associated Press |title=Earliest NFL draft takes place today |date=November 28, 1955 |page=3, part 2 }}{{Dead link|date=July 2026 |bot=InternetArchiveBot }}</ref>}}

This was the tenth year that the [[List of first overall National Football League Draft picks|first overall pick]] was a bonus pick determined by lottery. With the previous nine winners ineligible from the draw, only the [[Chicago Cardinals]], [[Green Bay Packers]], and [[Pittsburgh Steelers]] had an equal chance of winning.<ref>{{cite web|title=Draft History: 1940's |url=http://www.profootballhof.com/history/general/draft/1940s.aspx |publisher=[[Pro Football Hall of Fame]] |access-date=October 16, 2013 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20131001024342/http://www.profootballhof.com/history/general/draft/1940s.aspx |archive-date=October 1, 2013 |url-status=dead}}</ref> The draft lottery was won by Pittsburgh, who selected defensive back [[Gary Glick]].

